// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1640570486" "This is a very intriguing turn of events, {HeroName}. It seems my calculations were off about the Arachnos incursion.<br><br>I had believed your efforts in Atlas would deter them, but it seems it only served to fuel their anger to begin their invasion. Very curious.<br><br>I believe this will be the time where your true worth will be put to the test. Do you believe that you have the abilities to help push back the Arachnos attack?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - THIERY2VAR 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3284540379" "Arachnos will not stop until they've taken over all of Atlas. The situation is somewhat dire, you could say.<br><br>Most of the Freedom Phalanx are currently unable to help fight, whether it is due to the issues in Galaxy City or with threats by the <color yellow>Praetorians</color>.<br><br>The fate of Atlas is left in the hands of heroes such as yourself. Our goal will have to be to find where the main base of Arachnos is and strike at it."
// AcceptString :
"P1828055579" "We'll have to go after their leaders, then."
// SendOffString :
"P2171529051" "Correct. In order to find out where they are staging their attack from, we must strike down their higher ranking officials - their commanders.<br><br>I would suggest you go out and take the fight to them. It is possible that we may find information on them regarding the location of their main headquarters, or, at the very least, a method in which they are communicating to each other."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P721754997" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Commander</color>"

